WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.390
Do you have a big family, Angela?

2
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.510
No, I don’t.

3
00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.110
I live with my parents.

4
00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.970
I’m an only child.

5
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.380
Oh, I see.

6
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:24.320
Do you like being an only child?

7
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.560
Yes, I do.

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.220
It’s peaceful at home

9
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.840
And I can focus on what I do.

10
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.280
What about you?

11
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.460
Do you have any siblings?

12
00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.020
Yes, I do.

13
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.850
I have one older brother and two younger sisters.

14
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:46.390
Wow! That sounds like a big family.

15
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.590
Is it fun growing up with siblings?

16
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.390
Yes, it is!

17
00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.800
Sometimes it’s noisy.

18
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.740
But we always have fun together.

19
00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:58.210
We play football every weekend.

20
00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.450
My brother is my best friend.

21
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.630
That’s really nice.

22
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.940
I don’t have siblings.

23
00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.450
But I spend a lot of time with my cousins.

24
00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.050
That’s great.

25
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.970
What do your parents do?

26
00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.920
My father is a pilot.

27
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.860
He flies airplanes to different countries.

28
00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.710
That’s exciting!

29
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.640
What about your mother?

30
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.050
She is a chef.

31
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.470
She works at a restaurant downtown.

32
00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:28.220
Wow, that’s impressive!

33
00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.530
Does she cook at home, too?

34
00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.070
Yes, she does.

35
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.590
She makes amazing pasta on Sundays.

36
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.770
What about your parents?

37
00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:40.330
My father works at a bank.

38
00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.600
And my mother is a high school teacher.

39
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:45.720
That’s wonderful.

40
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.680
What do they like to do on weekends?

41
00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.970
My mom loves gardening.

42
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:54.860
She grows beautiful tomatoes.

43
00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:57.480
My dad enjoys reading.

44
00:01:57.670 --> 00:01:59.910
Sounds relaxing!

45
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.040
This Saturday, my family is having a big barbecue.

46
00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.370
Would you like to come?

47
00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.420
You can meet my family.

48
00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.030
I’d love to!

49
00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.820
Thank you, John.

50
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.100
Now let's learn some words about family.

51
00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:19.500
Parents

52
00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.080
Only child

53
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.150
Brother

54
00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:29.160
Sister

55
00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.620
Siblings

56
00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.650
Cousins
